  "ingredients": [
    "1 cup shortening",
    "1 cup white sugar",
    "1 cup packed brown sugar",
    "3 eggs",
    "4 cups all-purpose flour",
    "0.5 teaspoon salt",
    "1 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1 teaspoon baking soda",
    "2.5 cups dates, pitted and chopped",
    "0.5 cup white sugar",
    "1 cup water",
    "1 cup chopped walnuts"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/x-mARzaB5-eFMrTQeBJJerJyVu8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/10792-pinwheel-cookies-iii-ddmfs-01-10916-894a867997364924b44b03e066876c9b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/10792/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "To make the cookie dough: Beat butter, 1 cup white sugar, and brown sugar together in a large bowl until well combined. Add eggs, vanilla, flour, salt, and soda. Mix well, and set dough aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/9cy08iAzMqaI_xNRiZgRxQuAGcA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/10792-pinwheel-cookies-iii-ddmfs-03-10920-62c47aa046e844628e58f4b91fa17654.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/10792/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "To make the filling: Combine dates, sugar, water, and chopped nuts in a saucepan; cook and stir over medium heat until thickened. Cool filling. If necessary, add water until mixture can be spread easily on the dough.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/xWdWV5Jc890RM8zFdUhlf9iBf0U=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/10792-pinwheel-cookies-iii-ddmfs-04-10946-047d87f5999d42709bddbd14cae8f4ed.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/10792/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide dough into 4 parts. Roll out each piece on a floured surface to 1/2-inch thick. Spread with cooled, not cold filling.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Y09b8C2VqlbJezAUApZuNKi6im8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/10792-pinwheel-cookies-iii-ddmfs-06-10954-b0283d5033694effb4a726b0f0cbc600.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/10792/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roll up jelly-roll style; close ends and place rolls on cookie sheets. Refrigerate dough until cold, about 1 hour.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/G6UHckLI_DqpVsE1J2zgXRKWhw8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/10792-pinwheel-cookies-iii-ddmfs-07-10956-d44755ff6c644a7180ebdd1d578290bd.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/10792/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "When ready to bake, preheat the oven to 400 degrees F (205 degrees C). Slice chilled rolls, and place on a baking sheet.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/H8sBE2s6Bau10wnllhU-bwotbKU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/10792-pinwheel-cookies-iii-ddmfs-09-10990-163cfd1ae43b4ee89ccd83997b92e846.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/10792/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until edges are golden brown, about 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/D12gQnZXYzwv-HFTe-ZNfxxcZ28=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/10792-pinwheel-cookies-iii-ddmfs-10-11014-6fd0d6e92ab140a6a18bcc5798479acf.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/10792/step_07.webp"
    }
